Subject: [PATCH] Fix CSR reduction promotion, output dtype, and value strides

Resolve sum/product output dtype before dispatch, preserve explicit dtype in
accumulator allocation, and project the all-axis CUDA reduction into its
accumulator type. Products use the accumulator type on CPU and CUDA too.
Keep empty results structurally valid and retain both reduced dimensions.
Normalize values in pointer-based reducers: CSR values may be strided, unlike
its validated unit-stride index arrays. TensorIterator already handles strides.

